  "limits": [
    "Fourteen complete polynomial bilinear images pass the 1e-6 exact control-distance gate under an explicit normalized unit tensor chart. This does not qualify identical Rhino normal signs, UV orientation or physical knot domains. Raw comparison differences remain retained, without normalization or filtering.",
    "Coincident inputs and zero-width rectangles decline without creating history. Some collinear sets produce a nonzero rectangle in a deterministic containing plane. Repeated smallest singular values permit different optimal planes; general ambiguous inputs do not have qualified Rhino parity.",
    "The native N_FitPlaneToPts producer optimizes a bounding rectangle, while observed PlaneThroughPt uses normal-frame rectangular extents. The implementation reuses the existing shared faer fitter and tensor constructor; no new native C++ or independent plane solver is introduced.",
    "Fits retain the existing one-million-point cap and exact-rank/centering behavior. A finite unit normal and rounded origin represent the output plane; rounding or unrepresentable restored corners can reject. No proof work/tolerance limit is changed.",
    "Ninety-eight distinct focused Rust tests run in the default debug configuration, with 21 repeated release executions and 27 Python host/staging checks. Workspace clippy checks all targets with native-smlib enabled. No new sanitizer or performance qualification is claimed. The earlier preliminary two-command release run is not counted here.",
    "The retained licensed capture covers native geometry, output attributes and source/grip selection. Undo/Redo, cancellation and viewport dispatch are separately tested locally; native history and rendered preview parity are not claimed."
